## Code conventions

- `.NET 9`, C# latest features. Async everywhere that touches I/O.
- No external dependencies in `Common/` (RimAI.Core) — pure domain types only.
- Every new minister: own directory under `Src/Cabinet/<Name>/`.
- `Rules.cs` is first in every minister directory; must compile and have tests before LLM is wired.
- Fixture JSON files: `Src/Tests/<MinisterName>/Fixtures/`.
- Use `// TODO:` liberally for known gaps and deferred writes.

---

## Key constraints

- **Suggest by default.** MVP is suggest-only. See `Docs/design/advice.md`.
- **Output is `AdviceItem`s, not actions.** No RIMAPI write calls in MVP.
- **No direct minister-to-minister communication.** Flags only; CoS arbitrates.
- **LLMs on escalation only.** Rules handle the common case.
- **Dashboard is localhost-only.** Host binds `127.0.0.1`. Never `0.0.0.0`.
- **Deferred (M7+):** HTN planner, bulletin board, Labor solver, pawn-allocation writes.
